abstract: >-
  Reproducibility script for the numerical validation of the analytical
  bounds derived in "Function Space Analysis of Piecewise-Linear Energy
  Functionals under Lukasiewicz Fuzzy Semantics".  The script provides a
  Monte Carlo estimate of the log-partition function, an empirical
  reflected-Langevin mixing-time check, a Laplace-asymptotic verification,
  and an empirical scaling study of the total weight norm W as a function
  of the number of atoms n.  Self-contained: depends only on numpy and
  scipy; runs in under 60 s on a single CPU core; bit-reproducible under a
  fixed random seed.
keywords:
  - Lukasiewicz logic
  - Markov logic networks
  - Gibbs measures
  - Sobolev regularity
  - Bounded variation
  - Langevin dynamics
  - Poincare inequality
  - log-Sobolev inequality
  - neuro-symbolic AI
  - reproducibility
